  "notes": [
    "Emmalaan 4A-6 / Koningslaan 35 (pand 0363100012236822, built 1912): a flat-roofed brick block of two tall storeys over a raised ground storey, with a set-back rooftop addition; under renovation in the 2025 panoramas.",
    "walls[0] south-east front (panel 34, 10.2 m) and walls[1] south-west front (panel 62, 7.7 m): dark purple-brown brick, white-framed windows grouped in threes per bay on the two upper storeys, smaller windows in the raised ground storey, a white eaves overhang (cornice). walls[2] the north-east fronts (panels 1, 78, 65; crops w04-68w and w07-67w 2019-01-17, straight-on) show the same brick with windows in pairs. Those crops show the window groups and brick; the crops of these two fronts are 43-49 deg off square (w01-247L, w02-157L) or 40 % foliage (w03-247w), so the gate abstains on them.",
    "INFERRED: the remaining walls and the rooftop addition (otherWalls brick grid; 3DBAG roof planes)."
  ],
